WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.810 --> 00:00:02.240
- [Narrator] "Saved by the Bell" is a show

00:00:02.240 --> 00:00:04.430
that defined the '90s.

00:00:04.430 --> 00:00:06.635
Filled with topical lessons of the era.

00:00:06.635 --> 00:00:08.626
- There's no hope with dope!

00:00:08.626 --> 00:00:12.885
- [Narrator] And some
questionable fashion statements.

00:00:12.885 --> 00:00:15.290
But nothing's more memorable
than the theme song,

00:00:15.290 --> 00:00:16.943
and there's one guy to thank.

00:00:24.566 --> 00:00:27.550
Meet Scott Gale, the man
responsible for all the music

00:00:27.550 --> 00:00:28.900
for "Saved by the Bell."

00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:30.518
- I'm Scott Gale.

00:00:30.518 --> 00:00:31.351
(clock ringing)

00:00:31.351 --> 00:00:35.720
My resume would include 2,000
episodes of network television

00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:40.300
including "Saved by the Bell,"
"Golden Girls," "Empty Nest;"

00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:42.450
and there were some others in there.

00:00:42.450 --> 00:00:45.070
I first started getting
interested in music,

00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:46.670
when I saw Elvis Presley on television

00:00:46.670 --> 00:00:47.870
on "The Ed Sullivan Show."

00:00:51.250 --> 00:00:53.700
I said I want to do that, and
I was about five years old.

00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:56.713
Luckily my parents arranged
some guitar lessons for me.

00:00:57.650 --> 00:01:01.087
I first moved to LA in
1972; my first big break

00:01:01.087 --> 00:01:04.140
was music coordinator; I worked

00:01:04.140 --> 00:01:06.273
on every episode of "The Golden Girls."

00:01:09.800 --> 00:01:12.900
I got the first call at very
end of '89 from the producers

00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:14.930
about working on a new television show,

00:01:14.930 --> 00:01:16.950
and it was going to be
called "Saved by the Bell."

00:01:16.950 --> 00:01:20.410
They told me that it might
make seven episodes, maybe not.

00:01:20.410 --> 00:01:24.220
So, I put the phone
down, two minutes later

00:01:24.220 --> 00:01:25.991
the song came out of me.

00:01:25.991 --> 00:01:27.609
♪ By the time I grab my books ♪

00:01:27.609 --> 00:01:29.049
♪ And I give myself a look ♪

00:01:29.049 --> 00:01:32.239
♪ I'm at the corner just in
time to see the bus fly by ♪

00:01:32.239 --> 00:01:36.129
♪ It's alright 'cause
I'm saved by the bell ♪

00:01:36.129 --> 00:01:39.080
And it was like the luckiest
two minutes of my life.

00:01:39.080 --> 00:01:42.060
And when they heard mine, they
said, "That's it, that's it."

00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:43.880
I heard later that they did not want

00:01:43.880 --> 00:01:46.040
the name of the show in the title,

00:01:46.040 --> 00:01:47.980
but I did not get that note.

00:01:47.980 --> 00:01:50.410
"Saved by the Bell" was competing
with cartoons at the time

00:01:50.410 --> 00:01:53.960
because Saturday morning on
NBC there was no live-action

00:01:53.960 --> 00:01:57.980
for kids, so everything
needed to be brash and happy

00:01:57.980 --> 00:02:02.070
and lots of visual and lots of color.

00:02:02.070 --> 00:02:05.220
Peter Engel, the executive
producer, he always told us,

00:02:05.220 --> 00:02:08.280
"I want rock; I want it to be
happy; I want it to be driven;

00:02:08.280 --> 00:02:09.850
"and I want it to rock."

00:02:09.850 --> 00:02:12.734
No matter what the scene
was he wanted rock.

00:02:12.734 --> 00:02:15.067
(pop music)

00:02:17.130 --> 00:02:20.659
Most of the music was story oriented.

00:02:20.659 --> 00:02:22.992
(pop music)

00:02:27.139 --> 00:02:30.270
If there was a car crash
or a break up scene,

00:02:30.270 --> 00:02:33.000
we write to the picture;
and we even wrote rap.

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:35.750
We did the best we could;
I'm not really a rapper,

00:02:35.750 --> 00:02:38.540
but we laid down a beat
and the kids really,

00:02:38.540 --> 00:02:41.537
they made the songs come to life.

00:02:41.537 --> 00:02:43.870
(rap music)

00:02:46.420 --> 00:02:48.460
I really loved working
on "Saved by the Bell"

00:02:48.460 --> 00:02:51.600
because we had an opportunity to write

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:53.480
and perform so much music.

00:02:53.480 --> 00:02:56.620
A lot of people growing up in
the '90s, that was their show.

00:02:56.620 --> 00:02:59.640
People could relate to it;
I'm still a fan of the show.

00:02:59.640 --> 00:03:03.220
It comes on all the time; I
never get tired of watching it,

00:03:03.220 --> 00:03:06.339
and I never get tired of
seeing my name on the screen.

00:03:06.339 --> 00:03:11.172
♪ It's alright 'cause
I'm saved by the bell ♪

